  "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2, \\\\ 2x,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(-2,0)\\times (0,2)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (0,2).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}(x)({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)+(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}+2[{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
